  "scope": "Complete frozen-rule/source/reset/custom-kernel review, including exact full diff against independently audited merged #129 and current width/reset arithmetic; canonical source gate. No learner import or execution locally. Fresh initial GPU group is separate evidence.",
  "method": "Kernel-taught Ladder 60-768-512-256-10, AGOP^0.5 student coordinates, 480 Adam steps of batch 2500, current-training same-class tangent jitter, double-sampling of least-confident current queries late in training, 30 updates per CUDA graph replay, fused wide-combinator backward and class-symmetric teacher fallback. Native fused capturable Adam replaces foreach; LR .01378125.",
  "fresh_teacher": "teacher overwrites every cloned static training/query tensor before graph replay. sym_scores starts identity metric and zero PCG coefficients, computes both metric updates from current labels and refits with current-query predicted pseudo labels. Student metric and teacher scores are newly computed from supplied data every call.",
  "fresh_student": "ladder_kernel overwrites owned x/y/pool/ptar, refits tangents and hard-query IDs before reset. reset reinitializes all encoder/decoder/combinator parameters and biases/gain, clears Adam moments and step counts, update counter and loss-sampling scores, recreates all 480 minibatch index rows from current hard-query IDs and reseeds randomness. Scalar LR is overwritten from reset counter inside compiled fwd before every optimizer update.",
  "graph_and_optimizer": "CACHE preserves only compiled graphs/workspaces. Capture explicitly sets gradients to None for each of 30 steps, so all loss/backward/Adam work is captured. Sixteen graph replays perform 480 fixed updates on every call. Adam state tensor objects are retained but their values reset before fitting. Inference derives BN statistics again from current train rows. Fused Adam retains the same three per-parameter state tensors (step, exp_avg, exp_avg_sq), all cleared in reset. No scaler or AMSGrad is configured.",
  "guard_review": {
    "data": "Only current teacher scores, current student query labels and student errors on supplied training labels. No query truth or holdout/dataset identity is consulted.",
    "logic": "Counts confident teacher/student off-diagonal class confusions in a 10\u00d710 table, zeroes its diagonal and tests max count >60 or training mistakes >40. torch.where then selects confident teacher labels for every query row when triggered. Index structure and max are invariant to class relabeling.",
    "work": "Both teacher and student, all 480 updates, both query and train prediction passes execute before the guard regardless of whether it triggers; the output selection is branchless. Author statement that it often triggers on Fashion describes observed model behavior, not a dataset-based computational shortcut.",
    "status": "No static rule violation identified; actual holdout/time/dispersion gates are evaluated by the unchanged scorer."
  },
  "triton_review": "comb_bwd is registered at call time as a custom op with no mutated inputs; fake registration supplies shapes/dtypes for compile tracing only. Actual custom backward runs the Triton implementation. Phase 1 computes live combinator/BN adjoints and partial parameter/statistic sums; phase 2 reduces owned workspace and writes newly allocated gradient outputs. Kernel launch geometry uses GPU multiprocessor count for hardware partitioning. Current student widths 768/512/256 divide configured column blocks, so unmasked per-column metadata loads are in bounds; row tails are masked and workspace uses 20*S entries per chunk. No arbitrary external pointers, timer access or scorer mutation found. Width768 has12 column blocks of64; no column tails. All kernel bodies are byte-identical to the independently audited accepted #129 source.",
  "input_and_truth": "Original caller tensors receive no in-place writes. Teacher static tensors are clones; normalization/metric coordinates and tangent neighbor matrices are owned allocations. Query supervision comes from current teacher predictions and unlabeled reconstruction only; train label fit is allowed for guard/model selection.",
  "prior_or_bypass": "Only scalar hyperparameters, architecture/index lists and a four-entry launch-configuration dictionary; no stored fitted tensor/encoded pool, decoder, network, file read or parent/process introspection. os usage sets only compiler cache paths under /tmp. All graph side streams synchronize with current stream.",
